   {
    "id": "G07",
    "seg": "2 The dive",
    "shot": "S08",
    "text": "Cells move toward the groove, let go of their neighbours and slip underneath. Think of a crowd filing down a narrow ramp, then spreading out in the thin gap between two floors. Unlike a ramp, the groove is made of the cells themselves.",
    "facts": [
     "E05.01.03#f1"
